PHL-Patch-Reason: ord-multibyte
PHL-Patch-Kind: rewrite
PHL-Patch-Note: twig's html_attr escaper (Zend Framework's, adapted) walks every non-alphanumeric character of the subject through ord() under a /u regex, so a non-ASCII subject hands ord() a multi-byte string; php 8.5 deprecates that and answers the FIRST BYTE, which is what `$chr[0]` is. The match is never empty, so the two are the same value under php -- and without it the filter THROWS here for any non-ASCII input, which is a broken template output filter, not two test rows.

diff --git a/src/Extension/EscaperExtension.php b/src/Extension/EscaperExtension.php
index dee0f79f..9c169ad2 100644
--- a/src/Extension/EscaperExtension.php
+++ b/src/Extension/EscaperExtension.php
@@ -351,7 +351,7 @@ final class EscaperExtension extends AbstractExtension
                      * @license   https://framework.zend.com/license/new-bsd New BSD License
                      */
                     $chr = $matches[0];
-                    $ord = \ord($chr);
+                    $ord = \ord($chr[0]);
 
